  "prompt_mode": "short_sentence_continuation",
  "prompt_text": "Continue the text below with exactly one short, natural, coherent English sentence. Return only the continuation, with no preamble or explanation:\nA woman has been dating guy after guy, but it never seems to work out. She’s unaware that she’s actually been dating the same guy over and over; a shapeshifter who’s fallen for her, and is certain he’s going to get it right this time.\n\nOne day, the shapeshifter sees an advertisement for a seminar on how to be a better boyfriend. He thinks it is just the thing he needs to improve himself and make the woman really fall for him, so he signs up. When Clive, the shapeshifter, gets to the seminar, he start to wonder if this is really a good idea. The first sign he sees when he walk in says \"Be the real You.\" \"Really difficult,\" thought Clive. \"Especially when my whole existence involves being someone else.\"\n\nFrustrated, Clive starts to leave, when he notices a seminar going on in the next auditorium, with a similar theme. \"How to be a better girlfriend.\" And who does he see walking in, but Liz, the woman he has been in love with for ages. \"This is an interesting situation,\" thought Clive. Spurred on, that Liz thinks she needs help as much as he does, Clive strides into the auditorium with renewed purpose.",
  "reference_single_token_nfa_states": 18,
